ACKNOWLEDGMENTS
================

TOMMI — AI Agent Framework for the UNINOVIS European University Alliance

The first version of TOMMI was originally based on Tokki
(https://github.com/germtb/tokki/) by Gerard Moreno-Torres Bertran,
licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSES/MIT-Tokki.txt).

TOMMI has since been substantially extended and redesigned, including:
- RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) architecture with metadata-based
  retrieval and programmatic response paths
- LLM-based query classification with 12 intent categories
- Multi-agent support with configurable visibility, transparency levels,
  and reliability cues
- Inline interactive maps (Leaflet) for research output visualisation
- EU AI Act compliance features (audit logging, decision traces,
  crystal-box transparency)
- Support for multiple LLM providers (Mistral, Ollama, OpenAI)

This work has been supported by the UNINOVIS Data for L.I.F.E project
(EACEA/A/01.101177239) of the European Commission and the DC4EU project
co-funded by the European Union's Digital Europe Programme under Grant
Agreement no. 101102611.
